REVIEW-build-understanding-pass-host
commit 74f3aa7f1
what: split the row into five atomic rows (dm-pass-registry-field, REVIEW-build-recipe-check-seam, REVIEW-build-pass-assembly-injection, dm-pass-impls-move, REVIEW-audit-pass-host), ordered by dependency. No code changed; the children carry the work.
why: the row asked for one MOVE of the four *Pass impls + refuse_deferred + the test block + builtin() into understanding-host, but builtin() cannot leave corpus-engine while any corpus-engine site calls it (the engine may not name the host).
premise: measured 2026-09-18 on ralph/domains-campaign. git grep -n 'EnrichmentPassRegistry::builtin()' -- '*.rs' is TEN sites (engine/ingest.rs:1749,:1833, engine/mod.rs:2865,:3087, enrichment/pass.rs:469,:503,:539, recipe.rs:1903, recipe_parsing.rs:268, sovereign-tools/src/local_corpus/atlas_dispatch.rs:60). git grep -l 'Recipe::from_toml' is 34 files / 157 sites. CorpusEngine::new is 165 sites in 45 non-test files. understanding-host/Cargo.toml [dependencies] is empty. The four *Pass impl names appear nowhere outside enrichment/pass.rs (only a comment at engine/mod.rs:3095), so only builtin()'s callers move.
correction: the parent row's own check (LINT; LAYER; TEST(corpus-engine); TEST(understanding-host)) could not cover the cascade; corrected to "(minted; the children carry ...)" and the row marked done as a split. Recorded in ralph/DECISIONS.md 2026-09-18.
